  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"A short feedback card and a nearby collection box are available for readers leaving the service.\", \"decision\": \"How should feedback be gathered without slowing departures?\", \"goal\": \"Keep books moving and make the afternoon service easier to use without excluding readers who arrive without an appointment.\", \"problem\": \"A small library becomes crowded during afternoon pickups and returns. It has a request sheet, adjustable pickup windows, a few trained helpers, labeled shelves, and enough room to separate several activities. Staff want a practical plan that preserves walk-in access. Each decision below concerns a different part of the service; none requires exclusive use of all helpers or space.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nStaff hand readers a feedback card at collection and invite them to place it in the box on the way out. Readers can respond after the transaction has finished.\nA helper offers feedback cards near the exit and points readers to the collection box. The pickup desk does not need to introduce the feedback request.\nReaders take feedback cards from a stand beside the collection box after seeing a brief invitation near the exit. Feedback remains self-directed and separate from staff interactions."
    }
  ],
